From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally write the J604's Main
 words as macOS does

macOS 26B123 on the J604 starts the same firmware with a Main object
that differs from ours in 131 words besides its own pointers and
allocation records: a block of enable words around +0xe98 (where we
also set two that macOS leaves clear), the per-row scale and relative
tables, the state and core counts, and a run of later words. Which of
them matter is not known yet.

Add g16_main_macos (load time, default 0) with a built-in table of all
131 words as macOS has them, written into Main after the encoder, and
g16_main_macos_from / g16_main_macos_to to write only an index range of
it, so the set can be halved one boot at a time. The table assumes the
eleven-row table and is refused without it. Add g16_main_poke for
single words: "offset:value" pairs, at most 32, aligned and inside
Main, written last; a list that does not parse is ignored as a whole
and reported, and never fails the module load. With all of them unset
nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
